+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; ingredients
+  are consumed at `soldAt` with ref `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets already imported
+  are skipped. Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (dishes is the sum of
+  `qty` imported). A bad row answers `bad_request` and an item running out
+  answers `sale_out_of_stock` (409); both name the row (`row 2` is the first
+  data row) and nothing from the file is imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists per item
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }` for the days
+  `from`..`to` (inclusive): theoretical use from sales sold on those days,
+  actual use from every `consume` movement on those days, and
+  `difference = actual - theoretical`. Items where both are zero are left out.
